                <head>No. 37.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bayard to Sir L. S. Sackville
                            West</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Note verbale.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1888-04-21"><hi rendition="#italic">April</hi> 21,
                        1888</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Responding to the note verbale of Sir Lionel West, dated the 18th instant, it is
                    suggested on behalf of the United States that, as the cases of seizure of
                    British sealing vessels in Behring Sea, therein referred to, are now in court
                    pending an appeal from a judicial decision, it is preferable to await the
                    judgment of the appellate court in the premises.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
